# Files that belong in the repository but not in an installed copy.
# `specify extension add` copies the whole tree unless it is excluded here.

# The fixture is a whole fake spec-kit project, nested .specify/ and specs/
# included. Installing it under .specify/extensions/reconcile/ puts a second
# set of feature directories inside the user's project.
#
# This line is also load-bearing for the prompt itself. Spec Kit rewrites any
# relative path in a command body that names a directory present in the
# installed extension root (CommandRegistrar.rewrite_extension_paths), skipping
# only commands/, specs/ and dot-dirs. commands/reconcile.md contains example
# paths such as tests/integration/navigation.test.ts and src/router/index.ts.
# Ship a tests/ or src/ directory in the installed tree and those examples get
# silently rewritten to .specify/extensions/reconcile/... inside the prompt.
tests/

# Local agent and tooling configuration.
.claude/
.codemie/
.gitattributes

# Installing from a local path (`--dev`, or `init --extension <path>`) copies
# the tree verbatim, repository metadata included.
.git/
